# Env vars for snyk.just. Append into .env in your repo root (next to your justfile)
# and fill in the values you need. Add `set dotenv-load` to the top of your justfile so
# `just` loads it - module variables are resolved from the real OS environment, so
# `export X := "..."` in the justfile itself does NOT reach snyk.just; a real env var
# (shell or .env) does.
#
#   cat justfile-modules/snyk/.env.example.snyk >> .env
#
# See snyk.md for the full writeup of what each recipe does with these.

# --- optional (shown with their defaults) ---

# Snyk API token - only needed if you haven't authenticated via `snyk auth`.
# If set, it overrides the token stored in ~/.snyk by `snyk auth`.
#SNYK_TOKEN=your-token-here

# Directory to write Snyk reports to. The recipes create:
# - dependency.txt (from `snyk test --all-projects`)
# - code.txt (from `snyk code test`)
# - combined.txt (merged with metadata)
SNYK_REPORT_DIR=.snyk-reports

# Additional arguments passed to snyk commands. Useful for filtering projects,
# setting severity thresholds, or enabling org-level scans.
# Example: --severity-threshold=high --org=my-org
#SNYK_ADDITIONAL_ARGS=
